\title{Kruskal's Algorithm (with union-find)}
\date{2026-10-14T11:00:56Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\taxon{Algorithm}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{Given a [union-find](00P2) data structure, we can implement [Kruskal's Algorithm](00OX) as follows:

\pseudo{
  \state{\sf{Kruskal}#{(G):}}
  \indent{
  \state{#{T \gets} empty set of edges}
  \state{#{U \gets \sf{MakeSets}(V)}}
  \state{Sort the edges from smallest to biggest weight}
  \for{each edge #{e = (u,v)}}{
    \if{#{U.\sf{Find}(u) \neq U.\sf{Find}(v)}}{
      \state{Add #{e} to #{T}}
      \state{#{U.\sf{Union}(u,v)}}
    }
  }
  }
}

}
